  data: {
    LLM: "Block game: play a tile matching an open end of the layout or pass if unable. Tableau is built in a double line (matching end on the side). After each round, add pip total of unplayed tiles to each player's running score. At 101+ a player is eliminated unless they buy back (pay half stake, score set to middle of the other three). If all have 101+ (broken pool), scores reset to zero and everyone stakes again.",
    Player: "Block game: play a tile matching an open end of the layout or pass if unable. Tableau is built in a double line (matching end on the side). After each round, add pip total of unplayed tiles to each player's running score. At 101+ a player is eliminated unless they buy back (pay half stake, score set to middle of the other three). If all have 101+ (broken pool), scores reset to zero and everyone stakes again.",
    objective: 'Be the last player with a running score of 100 or less; players are eliminated at 101 or more. The last survivor collects the pool (Pulle).',
    gameplay: "Block game: play a tile matching an open end of the layout or pass if unable. Tableau is built in a double line (matching end on the side). After each round, add pip total of unplayed tiles to each player's running score. At 101+ a player is eliminated unless they buy back (pay half stake, score set to middle of the other three). If all have 101+ (broken pool), scores reset to zero and everyone stakes again.",
    keyRules: [
      'Four players, 7 tiles each; no boneyard.',
      'Pip total of unplayed tiles added to running score each round.',
      'Elimination at 101 or more; 100 is still in.',
      'Buy-back: pay half stake to pool, score becomes middle of other three.',
      'Broken pool: everyone 101+; scores reset, everyone stakes again.',
      'Last survivor wins the pool.',
    ],
